.\x00You got the BFG9000!  Oh, yes.\x00The vista opening ahead looks real damn\nfamiliar. Smells familiar, too -- like\nfried excrement. You didn\'t like this\nplace before, and you sure as hell ain\'t\nplanning to like it now. The more you\nbrood on it, the madder you get.\nHefting your gun, an evil grin trickles\nonto your face. Time to take some names.\x00W_Init: Init WADfiles.\x00Demo is from a different game version!\n(read %i, should be %i)\n\n*** You may need to upgrade your version of Doom to v1.9. ***\n    See: https://www.doomworld.com/classicdoom/info/patches.php\n    This appears to be %s.\x00Picked up the armor.\x00Suddenly, all is silent, from one horizon\nto the other. The agonizing echo of Hell\nfades away, the nightmare sky turns to\nblue, the heaps of monster corpses start \nto evaporate along with the evil stench \nthat filled the air. Jeeze, maybe you\'ve\ndone it. Have you really won?\n\nSomething rumbles in the distance.\nA blue light begins to glow inside the\nruined skull of the demon-spitter.\x00ST_Init: Init status bar.\x00Picked up a clip.\x00You gloat over the steaming carcass of the\nGuardian.  With its death, you\'ve wrested\nthe Accelerator from the stinking claws\nof Hell.  You relax and glance around the\nroom.  Damn!  There was supposed to be at\nleast one working prototype, but you can\'t\nsee it. The demons must have taken it.\n\nYou must find the prototype, or all your\nstruggles will have been wasted. Keep\nmoving, keep fighting, keep killing.\nOh yes, keep living, too.\x00You\'ve done it! The hideous cyber-\ndemon lord that ruled the lost Deimos\nmoon base has been slain and you\nare triumphant! But ... where are\nyou? You clamber to the edge of the\nmoon and look down to see the awful\ntruth.\n\nDeimos floats above Hell itself!\nYou\'ve never heard of anyone escaping\nfrom Hell, but you\'ll make the bastards\nsorry they ever heard of you! Quickly,\nyou rappel down to  the surface of\nHell.\n\nNow, it\'s on to the final chapter of\nDOOM! -- Inferno.\x00NOTE: Turning resolution is reduced; this is probably because there is a client recording a Vanilla demo.\x00M_Init: Init miscellaneous info.\x00 Doom Generic is free software, covered by the GNU General Public\n License.  There is NO warranty; not even for MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS\n FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. You are welcome to change and distribute\n copies under certain conditions. See the source for more information.\x00\nThis is not the registered version.\x00are you sure you want to end the game?\n\npress y or n.\x00quicksave over your game named\n\n\'%s\'?\n\npress y or n.\x00do you want to quickload the game named\n\n\'%s\'?\n\npress y or n.\x00are you sure? this skill level\nisn\'t even remotely fair.\n\npress y or n.\x00Picked up an energy cell.\x00Picked up a stimpack.\x00Picked up an energy cell pack.\x00you\'re lucky i don\'t smack\nyou for thinking about leaving.\x00M_StringJoin: Failed to allocate new string.\x00Even the deadly Arch-Vile labyrinth could\nnot stop you, and you\'ve gotten to the\nprototype Accelerator which is soon\nefficiently and permanently deactivated.\n\nYou\'re good at that kind of thing.\x00Betcha wondered just what WAS the hardest\nlevel we had ready for ya?  Now you know.\nNo one gets out alive.\x00\nP_Init: Init Playloop state.\x00I_Init: Setting up machine state.\x00i wouldn\'t leave if i were you.\ndos is much worse.\x00go ahead and leave. see if i care.\x00Time for a vacation. You\'ve burst the\nbowels of hell and by golly you\'re ready\nfor a break. You mutter to yourself,\nMaybe someone else can kick Hell\'s ass\nnext time around. Ahead lies a quiet town,\nwith peaceful flowing water, quaint\nbuildings, and presumably no Hellspawn.\n\nAs you step off the transport, you hear\nthe stomp of a cyberdemon\'s iron shoe.\x00Failed to open either \'%s\' or \'%s\' to write savegame.\x00Unknown or invalid IWAD file.\x00Picked up a yellow keycard.\x00Picked up a blue keycard.\x00Picked up a red keycard.\x00S_Init: Setting up sound.\x00You\'ve fought your way out of the infested\nexperimental labs.   It seems that UAC has\nonce again gulped it down.  With their\nhigh turnover, it must be hard for poor\nold UAC to buy corporate health insurance\nnowadays..\n\nAhead lies the military complex, now\nswarming with diseased horrors hot to get\ntheir teeth into you. With luck, the\ncomplex still has some warlike ordnance\nlaying around.\x00game saved.\x00External statistics registered.\x00BFG Edition: Using workarounds as needed.\x00 WARNING: You are playing using one of the Doom Classic\n IWAD files shipped with the Doom 3: BFG Edition. These are\n known to be incompatible with the regular IWAD files and\n may cause demos and network games to get out of sync.\x00ya know, next time you come in here\ni\'m gonna toast ya.\x00YOU HAVE WON! YOUR VICTORY HAS ENABLED\nHUMANKIND TO EVACUATE EARTH AND ESCAPE\nTHE NIGHTMARE.  NOW YOU ARE THE ONLY\nHUMAN LEFT ON THE FACE OF THE PLANET.\nCANNIBAL MUTATIONS, CARNIVOROUS ALIENS,\nAND EVIL SPIRITS ARE YOUR ONLY NEIGHBORS.\nYOU SIT BACK AND WAIT FOR DEATH, CONTENT\nTHAT YOU HAVE SAVED YOUR SPECIES.\n\nBUT THEN, EARTH CONTROL BEAMS DOWN A\nMESSAGE FROM SPACE: \"SENSORS HAVE LOCATED\nTHE SOURCE OF THE ALIEN INVASION. IF YOU\nGO THERE, YOU MAY BE ABLE TO BLOCK THEIR\nENTRY.  THE ALIEN BASE IS IN THE HEART OF\nYOUR OWN HOME CITY, NOT FAR FROM THE\nSTARPORT.\" SLOWLY AND PAINFULLY YOU GET\nUP AND RETURN TO THE FRAY.\x00Development mode ON.\x00I\'m OK.\x00YOU HAVE ENTERED DEEPLY INTO THE INFESTED\nSTARPORT. BUT SOMETHING IS WRONG. THE\nMONSTERS HAVE BROUGHT THEIR OWN REALITY\nWITH THEM, AND THE STARPORT\'S TECHNOLOGY\nIS BEING SUBVERTED BY THEIR PRESENCE.\n\nAHEAD, YOU SEE AN OUTPOST OF HELL, A\nFORTIFIED ZONE. IF YOU CAN GET PAST IT,\nYOU CAN PENETRATE INTO THE HAUNTED HEART\nOF THE STARBASE AND FIND THE CONTROLLING\nSWITCH WHICH HOLDS EARTH\'S POPULATION\nHOSTAGE.\x00CONGRATULATIONS, YOU\'VE FOUND THE SECRET\nLEVEL! LOOKS LIKE IT\'S BEEN BUILT BY\nHUMANS, RATHER THAN DEMONS. YOU WONDER\nWHO THE INMATES OF THIS CORNER OF HELL\nWILL BE.\x00What now? Looks totally different. Kind\nof like King Tut\'s condo. Well,\nwhatever\'s here can\'t be any worse\nthan usual. Can it?  Or maybe it\'s best\nto let sleeping gods lie..\x00You\'ve lost it...\x00Changing Level...\x00Next time, scumbag...\x00The loathsome spiderdemon that\nmasterminded the invasion of the moon\nbases and caused so much death has had\nits ass kicked for all time.\n\nA hidden doorway opens and you enter.\nYou\'ve proven too tough for Hell to\ncontain, and now Hell at last plays\nfair -- for you emerge from the door\nto see the green fields of Earth!\nHome at last.\n\nYou wonder what\'s been happening on\nEarth while you were battling evil\nunleashed. It\'s good that no Hell-\nspawn could have come through that\ndoor with you ...\x00The Gatekeeper\'s evil face is splattered\nall over the place.  As its tattered corpse\ncollapses, an inverted Gate forms and\nsucks down the shards of the last\nprototype Accelerator, not to mention the\nfew remaining demons.  You\'re done. Hell\nhas gone back to pounding bad dead folks \ninstead of good live ones.  Remember to\ntell your grandkids to put a rocket\nlauncher in your coffin. If you go to Hell\nwhen you die, you\'ll need it for some\nfinal cleaning-up ...\x00 WARNING: The loaded WAD file contains modified sprites or\n floor textures.  You may want to use the \'-merge\' command\n line option instead of \'-file\'.\x00ang=0x%x;x,y=(0x%x,0x%x)\x00Final Doom (alt)\x00timed %i gametics in %i realtics (%f fps)\x00%i.%i (unknown)\x00(null)\x00R_DrawPlanes: drawsegs overflow (%i)\x00R_DrawPlanes: opening overflow (%i)\x00R_DrawPlanes: visplane overflow (%i)\x00consistency failure (%i should be %i)\x00P_SpawnMapThing: Unknown type %i at (%i, %i)\x00Too many scrolling wall linedefs! (Vanilla limit is 64)\x00%s\n\n(press y to quit to dos.)\x00Unknown game version \'%s\'\x00Unknown configuration variable: \'%s\'\x00Invulnerability!\x00I\'m ready to kick butt!\x00please don\'t leave, there\'s more\ndemons to toast!\x00don\'t go now, there\'s a \ndimensional shambler waiting\nat the dos prompt!\x00look, bud. you leave now\nand you forfeit your body count!\x00P_StartButton: no button slots left!\x00P_RemoveActivePlat: can\'t find plat!\x00A chainsaw!  Find some meat!\x00P_AddActivePlat: no more plats!\x00Picked up the MegaArmor!\x00Weird actor->movedir!\x00\nYou cannot -file with the shareware version. Register!\x00don\'t leave yet -- there\'s a\ndemon around that corner!\x00You got the rocket launcher!\x00Help!\x00Picked up a backpack full of ammo!\x00%s is turbo!\x00You got the super shotgun!\x00You got the shotgun!\x00You got the chaingun!\x00You got the plasma gun!\x00level 11: \'o\' of destruction!\x00Berserk!\x00You suck!\x00Z_ChangeUser: Tried to change user for invalid block!\x00the spider mastermind must have sent forth\nits legions of hellspawn before your\nfinal confrontation with that terrible\nbeast from hell.  but you stepped forward\nand brought forth eternal damnation and\nsuffering upon the horde as a true hero\nwould in the face of something so evil.\n\nbesides, someone was gonna pay for what\nhappened to daisy, your pet rabbit.\n\nbut now, you see spread before you more\npotential pain and gibbitude as a nation\nof demons run amok among our cities.\n\nnext stop, hell on earth!\x00you want to quit?\nthen, thou hast lost an eighth!\x00let\'s beat it -- this is turning\ninto a bloodbath!\x00You\'ve bashed and battered your way into\nthe heart of the devil-hive.  Time for a\nSearch-and-Destroy mission, aimed at the\nGatekeeper, whose foul offspring is\ncascading to Earth.  Yeah, he\'s bad. But\nyou know who\'s worse!\n\nGrinning evilly, you check your gear, and\nget ready to give the bastard a little Hell\nof your own making!\x00if i were your boss, i\'d \n deathmatch ya in a minute!\x00MegaSphere!\x00Come here!\x00Supercharge!\x00Doom 1.2 does not have a version code!\x00I\'m not looking too good!\x00W_GetNumForName: %s not found!\x00IWAD file \'%s\' not found!\x00Picked up a medikit that you REALLY need!\x00level 20: gotcha!\x00$`\\!\x00%s:%i: Z_ChangeTag: block without a ZONEID!\x00R_ProjectSprite: invalid sprite number %i \x00R_ProjectSprite: invalid sprite frame %i : %i \x00Indigo: \x00Brown: \x00Green: \x00Red: \x00Z_Init: Init zone memory allocation daemon. \x00R_Init: Init DOOM refresh daemon - \x00fuck %d \r\x00Z_CheckHeap: two consecutive free blocks\n\x00Using %s for configuration and saves\n\x00Using %s for savegames\n\x00Trying IWAD file:%s\n\x00saving config in %s\n\x00 couldn\'t open %s\n\x00 adding %s\n\x00Unknown gfxmode value: %s\n\x00\tdefault file: %s\n\x00        extra configuration file: %s\n\x00\t%s\n\x00Z_CheckHeap: next block doesn\'t have proper back link\n\x00Z_CheckHeap: block size does not touch the next block\n\x00SpechitOverrun: Warning: unable to emulatean overrun where numspechit=%i\n\x00startskill %i  deathmatch: %i  startmap: %i  startepisode: %i\n\x00zone memory: %p, %x allocated for zone\n\x00saveg_write8: Error while writing save game\n\x00saveg_read8: Unexpected end of file while reading save game\n\x00Wad file %s doesn\'t have IWAD or PWAD id\n\x00I_InitGraphics: DOOM screen size: w x h: %d x %d\n\x00G_CheckSpot: unexpected angle %d\n\x00I_InitGraphics: Auto-scaling factor: %d\n\x00I_InitGraphics: Scaling factor: %d\n\x00I_InitGraphics: framebuffer: x_res: %d, y_res: %d, x_virtual: %d, y_virtual: %d, bpp: %d\n\x00I_InitGraphics: framebuffer: RGBA: %d%d%d%d, red_off: %d, green_off: %d, blue_off: %d, transp_off: %d\n\x00M_Episode: 4th episode requires UltimateDOOM\n\x00Playing demo %s.\n\x00EV_VerticalDoor: Tried to close something that wasn\'t a door.\n\x00Game mode indeterminate.  No IWAD file was found.  Try\nspecifying one with the \'-iwad\' command line parameter.\n\x00EV_DoDonut: WARNING: emulating buffer overrun due to NULL back sector. Unexpected behavior may occur in Vanilla Doom